  message: "CORRECTION, and it supersedes the mangled entry immediately above (backticks in\na double-quoted shell arg were substituted and ate two lines -- the recorded\nlandmine, hit anyway). Full text follows; the previous entry should be read as\nreplaced by this one.\n\nTHE MECHANISM AS FILED IS CONFIRMED. THE CONSEQUENCE I DREW FROM IT WAS WRONG,\nAND THE FIX IS FAR SMALLER THAN OPTION 1.\n\nWHAT FORCED THE RE-TEST. The owner: \"it was working a while without issue on\ngithub though so i dont know why things started piling up these past 2-3 days.\"\nThat is inconsistent with \"GitHub never honored merge=union\" being a NEW problem,\nso the mechanism was re-measured rather than defended.\n\nMECHANISM, CONFIRMED on .INV-juvul-*.ops for tracker-sync/20260824-160016:\n    merge-base (dev when the branch was cut)   32 lines\n    branch tip                                 54 lines  (+22 appended)\n    current dev                                61 lines  (+29 DIFFERENT appended)\nBoth sides appended at the END of one append-only file from a common base.\nmerge=union resolves that trivially client-side; GitHub's plain three-way merge\nsees two different additions at one location and calls it a conflict.\n\nSo nothing broke recently. While syncs merged PROMPTLY, dev never diverged on\nthose files before the PR landed. The moment one PR sits unmerged and any other\nsync appends to the same file, that PR becomes PERMANENTLY unmergeable\nserver-side. The Sept 1-2 axis campaign (WI-kurod / WI-kijup / WI-mubup) plus\nINV-foluz drove heavy tracker throughput, which is why the window slammed shut\nnow rather than earlier.\n\n*** THE PART I GOT WRONG, AND IT REVERSES THE ACTION. *** This item said the five\nbranches need merging, and proposed rebasing auto-sync. Measured instead, two\nindependent ways:\n\n  set difference over every file each branch touches, branch vs current dev:\n      20260824-160016   0 lines not already in dev\n      20260830-015453   0\n      20260901-014222   0\n      20260901-014517   0\n      20260902-015521   0\n\n  trial merge (git merge-tree --write-tree) against origin/dev, tree compared to\n  origin/dev's own tree 1b702f249a:\n      ALL FIVE produce an IDENTICAL tree.\n\nThey are COMPLETE NO-OPS. Every op they carry is already in dev.\n\nWHY, AND IT IS THE GOOD NEWS: THE DURABILITY GUARANTEE IS INTACT. When a sync\nfails to merge, its ops stay in the local working tree -- WI-lufal deliberately\ngates the destructive post-sync cleanup on merge success -- so the NEXT sync\nrebuilds from a freshly fetched origin/dev and carries them forward. The DATA\nalways gets through. What is left behind is litter, not stranded ops.\n\nACTION: CLOSE ALL FIVE PRs. Do not merge them, do not rebase anything, and do\nnot touch merge=union. There is nothing to recover and no code change is needed\nfor the repair itself.\n\nRE-SCOPED REMEDY, much smaller than options 1-3 as filed. Auto-sync does not\nclean up its own superseded branches. The whole fix is a prune step: for each\nopen tracker-sync branch, if a trial merge against origin/dev yields a tree equal\nto origin/dev's tree, the branch is superseded and its PR can be closed. That\npredicate is the exact no-op test used above, it is decidable locally with no API\nguessing, and by construction it cannot close a branch carrying unique ops.\n\nOPTION 1 (rebase before push) IS WITHDRAWN AS UNNECESSARY. do_sync already builds\neach sync commit on a freshly fetched origin/dev via plumbing (read-tree from\nbase_sha at sync.py:1395-1410), so a NEW sync is never stale. Only ABANDONED\nbranches go stale, and closing them is the answer to that. The owner's instinct\nthat the rebase change looked major was right, and the measurement makes it moot."  # d6da
