- op: discuss  # 1674
  at: '2026-09-02T18:32:22Z'  # 1674
  by: agent  # 1674
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1674
  clock: 7  # 1674
  nonce: '1674'  # 1674
  message: "SHIPPED as PR #713 (merged, dev c8de5b2b30). Recording the closure evidence that\nwas owed and missing: the work landed but this thread stopped at the diagnosis.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, not a proxy. The remedy is the prune step described above,\nbuilt at two entry points:\n\n  scripts/tracker sync --prune        explicit, handled BEFORE preflight_check\n  _maybe_auto_sync                    automatic, after every successful auto-sync\n\nfind_superseded_sync_branches uses the exact predicate filed above: for each open\ntracker-sync/* branch, git merge-tree --write-tree against origin/dev, and the\nbranch is superseded iff the resulting tree equals origin/dev's own tree. By\nconstruction it cannot close a branch carrying a unique op.\n\nRUN LIVE after merge, with the owner's approval to let a sync close PRs:\n  9 superseded branches detected, 9 PRs closed (including #682, #683, #706 that\n  the owner reported), all 9 remote tracker-sync branches deleted, queue at 0.\nThe tracker-sync PR queue has been at zero since; it was last at zero before\nAugust 24.\n\nWHAT THE BUILD ITSELF TAUGHT, kept because it cost a rework. The prune was first\nwired into do_sync's post-merge path and killed 23 tests that script an exact\nsequence of _git calls. That was the wrong-layer signal, not brittle tests:\ndo_sync implements a TRANSACTION, and litter collection is not part of it.\nMoving up one layer to _maybe_auto_sync fixed all 23 -- and the rationale I had\ngiven for the original placement (a lock held there) turned out not to be\nload-bearing at all.\n\nOption 1 (rebase before push) stays WITHDRAWN as unnecessary, per the analysis\nabove. merge=union was not touched."  # 1674
